  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n500mb analysis reveals the subtropical ridge remains in dominant\ncontrol over the southwest US today. Temperatures today continue \nto be well above average, with further warming expected for \nSaturday. Temperatures peak this weekend with high temperatures \nabout 10 degrees above normal. Slightly elevated moisture is also\nlimiting overnight cooling and keeping low temperatures quite \nmild as well. This is bringing widespread moderate HeatRisk and \nlocally major HeatRisk in and west of the mountains, with \nwidespread major HeatRisk in the deserts. The Extreme Heat Warning\nand Heat Advisory remains in effect through Monday evening and \ncontain specifics on temperatures.\n\nThis dominant upper level high pressure slowly drifts east and\ngradually weakens into Tuesday, bringing a relative cooling trend\nwith high temperatures near 5 degrees above normal for Tuesday.\nEnsembles are in fairly good agreement that the ridge will \nrestrengthen after Wednesday and move westward with the center \nnear Las Vegas for late next week. High temperatures on Wednesday\nwill range from the mid 70s to around 80 near the coast to the \nmid 90s to 102 for the Inland Empire with 108 to 112 for the lower\ndeserts. This will be followed by a warming trend through the end\nof July into the first weekend in August.",
